inkedin.com/company/amazon) Interview Experience — Round 1 (SDE-2)\\n\\nLast year, I interviewed with [Amazon](https://linkedin.com/company/amazon) for the SDE-2 role, and Round 1 was a deep dive into Data Structures & Algorithms + Leadership Principles.\\n\\n🔍 What was asked?\\n\\nThe coding questions were variations of well-known problems:\\n• 📌 Maximum Profit in Job Scheduling\\nhttps://lnkd.in/g--NmUZc https://lnkd.in/gDW8Rbs4\\n• 📌 Max Consecutive Ones III\\nhttps://lnkd.in/g--NmUZc https://lnkd.in/gWH5nDaV\\n\\n⏱️ Round structure (60 mins)\\n• 💻 40 minutes — Coding (approach, optimization, edge cases)\\n• 💬 20 minutes — Leadership Principles (LPs)\\n\\nCheckout this to boost your selection chances: https://lnkd.in/g--NmUZc\\n\\n👉 Key takeaway:\\nFor [Amazon](https://linkedin.com/company/amazon), DSA alone is NOT enough.\\nYour interviewer equally evaluates:\\n• How you think\\n• How you make decisions\\n• How you’ve handled real-world situations\\n\\nIf you’re targeting [Amazon](https://linkedin.com/company/amazon) SDE-2, prepare Leadership Principles with real stories (STAR method) as seriously as you prepare LeetCode.\\n\\n📌 I’ll keep sharing [Amazon](https://linkedin.com/company/amazon) interview insights, preparation tips, and system design learnings.\\n\\n➡️ Follow [SHIVAM SOMANI](https://linkedin.com/in/shivam-99-somani) for more such updates.\\n\\n#[Amazon](https://linkedin.com/company/amazon) #SDE2 #InterviewExperience #DSA #LeadershipPrinciples #TechCareers #CareerJourney #Amazon\\n\\n![💼 My Amazon Interview Experience — Round 1 (SDE-2) | SHIVAM SOMANI image](https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D5622AQESo6iG6IiQug/feedshare-image-high-res/B56Z3uep40I8AU-/0/1777822506846?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=WMYl_NLU_vYZO4xxmFr_eNBFCZq8HwlaLctseqgYMcw)\\n\\n## Comments\\n\\n**[Anandnarayanan S](https://linkedin.com/in/anand-data)** · 2026-05-04\\n> ++\\n\\n**[Aryan Gupta](https://linkedin.com/in/aryan-gupta-81887028a)** · 2026-05-04 · 1 reaction\\n> Helpful share\\n\